title: Polyethylene
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The most common plastic. Bags, bottles, cling film, and the coating inside a paper cup.

Made from oil and gas.

It keeps water out, which is why it lines a [[Tetra Pak]] carton. People take that lining for wax.

By itself it can be melted and remolded. See [[Precious Plastics]] and [[3p: People Processing Plastic]]. Bonded to paper or foil, it becomes part of a [[Monstrous Hybrid]].

See [[PolyAl]], [[Plasticshed]]
